; RKE2's policy labels /opt/cni for the containers that install CNI plugins there, among them RKE2's
; Cilium's portmap installer, which runs confined and may write only into container files. An
; image-mode node keeps /opt in /var/opt, which this labels alike wherever the policy does not
; already take /var/opt for /opt.
(filecon "/var/opt/cni(/.*)?" any (system_u object_r container_file_t ((s0) (s0))))
